        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b996d694-07a5-5d5b-a105-05777d8df35a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, Washington Township\n- Roads: Pennsylvania Route 380, Pennsylvania Route 780, Interstate 579\n- Landmarks: PPG Paints Arena, UPMC Mercy\n- Organizations: Pittsburgh Penguins, National Hockey League, Pittsburgh Power, Arena Football League, University of Pittsburgh Medical Center, Duquesne University\n\nFacts:\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is officially designated SR 400 because Interstate 380 exists elsewhere in Pennsylvania.\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is also known as the J.F. Bonetto Memorial Highway and, within Pittsburgh, as Bigelow Boulevard, Baum Boulevard, and Frankstown Road.\n- Pennsylvania Route 380 is a 32.80-mile state highway in western Pennsylvania.\n- The western terminus of Pennsylvania Route 380 is at Interstate 579 in downtown Pittsburgh near PPG Paints Arena.\n- Pennsylvania Route 780 has its eastern terminus at Pennsylvania Route 380 in Washington Township.\n- From 2011 to 2014, PPG Paints Arena was the home of the Pittsburgh Power of the Arena Football League.\n- PPG Paints Arena is a multi-purpose indoor arena in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\n- PPG Paints Arena serves as the home of the Pittsburgh Penguins of the National Hockey League.\n- UPMC Mercy is a main hospital facility of the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center in the Uptown section of Pittsburgh, adjacent to Duquesne University.\n- UPMC Mercy is a few blocks from PPG Paints Arena and downtown Pittsburgh.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4ca454e8-8db6-52d4-931d-8bea8faee31b",
        "text": "Page: Pennsylvania Route 380. Sentence: Pennsylvania Route 380 (officially, SR 400 because of I-380 elsewhere in Pennsylvania), also known as J.F. Bonetto Memorial Highway and within the city of Pittsburgh Bigelow Boulevard, Baum Boulevard and Frankstown Road, is a 32.80 mi long state highway in western portions of the U.S. state of Pennsylvania.\nPage: Pennsylvania Route 380. Sentence: The western terminus of the route is at Interstate 579 in downtown Pittsburgh near PPG Paints Arena.\nPage: PPG Paints Arena. Sentence: PPG Paints Arena is a multi-purpose indoor arena in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania that serves as home to the Pittsburgh Penguins of the National Hockey League (NHL), and was the home of the Pittsburgh Power of the Arena Football League (AFL) from 2011 to 2014.\nPage: Pennsylvania Route 780. Sentence: The eastern terminus is at PA 380 in Washington Township.\nPage: UPMC Mercy. Sentence: UPMC Mercy is a main hospital facility of the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC) and is located in the Uptown section of the city of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, adjacent to Duquesne University, and a few blocks from the PPG Paints Arena and downtown Pittsburgh.",
